.env
.env.*
!.env.example
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
*.backup
*.backup.*

# Conversation/memory dumps — may contain credentials & personal context.
# Kept local only, never committed (Vinta directive 2026-06-09).
memory/*.md

# Android signing key — NEVER commit
android-twa/android.keystore
android-twa/*.aab
android-twa/*.apk
android-twa/app/
android-twa/build/
android-twa/.gradle/

# ── COUNCIL RUNTIME JUNK (2026-08-30) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Every seat runs in its own git worktree, and the council writes these INTO the
# worktree at runtime. They were never ignored, so all 12 seat worktrees showed
# as dirty permanently — which made the new merge-back guard SKIP every one of
# them (it refuses to merge a dirty tree, correctly, since merging would silently
# drop uncommitted work). Net effect: finished work could never ship. These are
# machine state, not source; ignoring them is what lets real work through.
.claude/
.council-born-agents/
